# Dockerfile line 16 is `ADD . /go-ethereum`, so everything not excluded here
# lands in the BUILDER layer. The final image is unaffected — it is multi-stage
# and only does `COPY --from=builder .../geth` — but the builder layer is still
# reachable via `docker build --target builder`, `docker save`, and
# `buildx --cache-to=type=registry`.
#
# This file is the second half of the same private/public gate as .gitignore.
# Keep the two reconciled: anything secret enough to keep out of a commit is
# secret enough to keep out of a build context.
#
# SYNTAX IS NOT GITIGNORE SYNTAX. Two differences that matter here, per
# docker/docs `build/concepts/context.md`:
#   1. "Leading and trailing slashes in ignore patterns are disregarded" — so
#      `/foo/`, `/foo`, `foo/` and `foo` are one and the same pattern.
#   2. A bare pattern is matched against the path from the context ROOT, so it
#      does NOT match at any depth the way gitignore's does. Depth needs `**/`.
# Consequence: `keystore` below excludes only a root-level keystore directory.
# It must stay that way — `accounts/keystore/` is 32 tracked Go source files
# the build needs, and a `**/keystore` pattern would break the build.

**/*_test.go

build/_workspace
build/_bin
tests/testdata

# Local working directory — holds this machine's live P2P node keys
# (.local/classic-nodekey, .local/mordor-nodekey) and internal working docs.
.local
local

# Agent instruction files that are machine-local by design
CLAUDE.local.md
**/*.local.md
.claude

# Secrets & credentials. `**/` prefixes give depth coverage; verified safe
# because the tracked tree contains no *.pem, *.key or .env file at any depth.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
**/credentials.json
**/service-account.json
secrets

# Blockchain & crypto. `keystore` is root-only on purpose — see the syntax note
# at the top. The node keys this actually defends live under .local/, already
# excluded above.
keystore
**/*.keystore
**/wallet.json
**/mnemonic.txt
**/nodekey
**/*nodekey
**/jwt.hex
**/jwtsecret

# Build-context weight, with no effect on the produced binary: `geth` is a
# stale ~75 MB root binary (already gitignored) and `git.diff` is ~6 MB of
# inert text. Neither is read by the build.
geth
git.diff

# NOTE: `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded, though it is ~1.5 GB of the build
# context. `build/ci.go install` calls internal/build.LocalEnv(), which reads
# .git/HEAD to embed the commit hash and date via -ldflags. Without .git it
# degrades gracefully rather than failing — env.Commit comes back empty and
# ci.go:257 simply skips those flags — so the build still succeeds and the
# binary silently loses its version metadata. Excluding it is a real trade
# against release-artifact provenance, not free weight, and is a decision for
# the maintainer rather than a wiring change.
